# 3. NON-NEGOTIABLE PRODUCTION REQUIREMENTS

The following rules apply throughout the project.

## Real data only

- Use a real production database.
- Persist all important business records.
- Never use hardcoded dashboard statistics.
- Never populate production screens with fake records.
- Never create fake activity logs.
- Never create fake analytics.
- Never fabricate publishing statuses.
- Never display sample agent executions as real executions.
- Do not silently fall back to mock data when an API fails.
- Make empty states clear and informative.
- Seed only essential system configuration, roles, permissions, and reference data.
- If development fixtures are needed, isolate them from production and make their use explicit.

## Real operations only

Every interactive element must have an actual implemented behavior.

Examples:
- Creating a client must create a database record.
- Assigning an agent must create an actual task assignment.
- Running an agent must invoke a real configured AI provider.
- Generating an image must call an actual image-generation provider.
- Generating a video must call an actual video-generation provider.
- Approving content must create an immutable approval record.
- Scheduling content must create a persistent publishing job.
- Publishing must call the actual platform API.
- Analytics must be retrieved from connected platform accounts.
- Deleting a record must execute an authorized deletion or archival operation.

No decorative buttons, fake progress indicators, fake notifications, or simulated backend responses.

## Evidence-based completion

An operation can only be marked completed when:
- The operation actually executed.
- The backend validated its result.
- Required outputs were persisted.
- The execution record was saved.
- Any relevant external identifier or evidence was recorded.

For example, a successful publishing operation should store:
- Connected social account ID.
- External platform post ID.
- Published URL when available.
- Actual publication timestamp.
- API response metadata.
- Publishing job ID.
- Final execution status.

## Honest integration status

Each integration must have a real status:
- Not configured.
- Configuration incomplete.
- Connected.
- Authentication expired.
- Permission denied.
- Temporarily unavailable.
- Error.
- Disconnected.

Never show an integration as connected before validating its credentials and permissions.

