# 7. HUMAN APPROVAL AND GOVERNANCE

The platform must operate using a hybrid human-plus-AI management model.

Agents perform routine work autonomously within their permissions.

Humans approve important decisions and external side effects.

Mandatory approval gates include:

- Client strategy approval when required.
- Content calendar approval when required.
- Final content approval before publishing.
- Brand identity changes.
- External publishing.
- Financial spending.
- Advertising spend.
- Client pricing.
- Contracts.
- Sensitive data deletion.
- New integration authorization.
- Agent permission changes.
- New tools with external side effects.

## Immutable approval model

An approval must reference:
- Exact content ID.
- Exact content version ID.
- Reviewer ID.
- Approval decision.
- Approval timestamp.
- Reviewer comments.
- Relevant attachments.
- Version hash where appropriate.

Possible decisions:
- Approved.
- Rejected.
- Changes requested.

If content changes materially after approval, invalidate the previous approval and require a new one.

Do not permit an agent to approve its own work when human approval is required.

