# 28. DEFINITION OF DONE

The system is not complete simply because the UI looks finished.

A feature is complete only when:
- Its frontend exists.
- Its backend exists.
- Its database operations work.
- Its authorization works.
- Its validation works.
- Its errors are handled.
- Its tests pass.
- Its execution is observable.
- Its documentation exists.

The overall system cannot be called production-ready until the following critical path has been demonstrated in a real, authorized environment:

### Required end-to-end acceptance test

1. An administrator logs in.
2. The administrator creates a real client.
3. A real brand profile is saved.
4. A real project is created.
5. A real social account is connected through official authorization.
6. An AI agent receives an actual task.
7. The agent calls a real configured AI model.
8. The agent produces real content.
9. Actual media is generated or uploaded.
10. The content passes validation.
11. A human reviews and approves the exact content version.
12. The publishing system schedules the approved version.
13. A real publishing API call is made.
14. The external platform confirms the publication.
15. The external post ID and URL are saved.
16. Analytics are retrieved from the actual platform when available.
17. Costs and execution records are persisted.
18. The complete activity history can be inspected.

If any external integration requires additional credentials, account eligibility, platform approval, or manual authorization, report that dependency explicitly.

Do not falsely mark the acceptance test as passed.

